 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532665,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A rectangular solid has a width of 6 cm, length of 15 cm, and height or depth of 6 cm. Find the surface area and the volume.<br>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/98cb27f35870214d.png\" alt=\"A rectangular prism with its length, width, and height marked 15 centimeters, 6 centimeters, and 6 centimeters.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\begin{array}{rcl}{SA}&amp;{ = }&amp;{432\\text{ cm}{^2}}\\\\{V}&amp;{ = }&amp;{540\\text{ cm}{^3}}\\\\ \\end{array}\">\\begin{array}{rcl}{SA}&amp;{ = }&amp;{432\\text{ cm}{^2}}\\\\{V}&amp;{ = }&amp;{540\\text{ cm}{^3}}\\\\ \\end{array}</span>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The surface area of a right prism where <i>B</i> is the area of the base, <i>p</i> is the perimeter of the base, and <i>h</i> is the height is <span data-math=\"SA = 2B + ph\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The rectangular base has an area <span data-math=\"{\\text{ =  LW  =  (6 cm) (15 cm)  =  90 c}}{{\\text{m}}^{\\text{2}}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The perimeter of the base <span data-math=\"{\\text{ =  }}p{\\text{  =  2(6 cm)  +  2(15 cm)  =  42 cm}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The surface area <span data-math=\" = {\\text{ }}2B + ph = {\\text{ }}2\\left( {90{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}} \\right){\\text{ }} + {\\text{ }}\\left( {42{\\text{ cm}}} \\right)\\left( {6{\\text{ cm}}} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}180{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2} + {\\text{ }}252{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2} = {\\text{ }}432{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The surface area is 432 square centimeters.</p>\n<p>The volume of a right prism is <span data-math=\"V = Bh\\ = {\\text{ }}\\left( {90{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}} \\right)\\left( {6{\\text{ cm}}} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}540{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^3}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The volume is 540 cubic centimeters.</p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
